      ],
      "source": "https://sewardtownshipil.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before its 1850 renaming, the township was known as Franklin, reflecting its early settlers’ New York roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://sewardtownshipil.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Rock Island Railroad once ran through Seward, but its line was diverted to Morris and later Minooka, reshaping local trade routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://kendallkin.org/county-history/town-histories/seward-township/reminiscences-seward.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Route 52 cuts east‑west across Seward, while Interstate 80 borders the township’s southern edge, linking it to the broader region.",
